  "steps": [
    "If using breasts, slice each in half horizontally so the pieces are an even 1/2 to 3/4 inch thick. Mix the buttermilk, hot sauce, 1/2 tsp salt, and 1/4 tsp pepper in a bowl, add the chicken, cover, and refrigerate at least 4 hours or overnight.",
    "Slaw: mix the cabbage, mayonnaise, vinegar, sugar, salt, and pepper. Refrigerate while you cook.",
    "Set up the breading: lift the chicken out of the marinade and keep the marinade in its bowl. In a second shallow bowl, whisk the flour, cornstarch, garlic powder, paprika, cayenne, 1 tsp salt, and 1/2 tsp pepper.",
    "Dredge each piece in the flour mix, dip back into the buttermilk, then into the flour mix again, pressing to coat. Rest on a rack for 10 minutes.",
    "Heat 2 inches of oil in a heavy pot or Dutch oven to 325 to 350°F. Fry the chicken until deep golden and 165°F inside, 5 to 7 minutes per side for thighs (less for thin breast cutlets). Drain on a wire rack.",
    "Carefully ladle 1/3 cup of the hot frying oil into a heatproof bowl and whisk in the cayenne, brown sugar, garlic powder, paprika, and chili powder until smooth.",
    "Brush the glaze generously over both sides of the chicken while it is still hot.",
    "Toast the cut sides of the buns in the butter in a skillet over medium heat, then build with pickles, chicken, and slaw."
  ],
  "tips": [
    "If the frying oil tastes burnt, make the glaze with melted butter or half butter, half oil instead."
  ],
